# SCAR — recall before you edit

Before applying a non-trivial edit, call `scar_recall` with the current file and the error/task. If SCAR returns hits, obey active corrections. If it abstains, proceed normally.

Do not invent a house rule when SCAR has nothing stored.

## How to call it

- MCP tool: `scar_recall` with `repo_id`, `file_path`, and optional `symbol`, `error_text`, `task_text`.
- CLI: `scar recall --repo <id> --file <path> [--symbol NAME] [--error TEXT] [--task TEXT]`
- HTTP: `POST /v1/recall` with `{repo_id, file_path, symbol, error_text, task_text}`

## After you are corrected

Record the instruction immediately with `scar_record` (MCP), `scar record --repo --file --correction` (CLI), or `POST /v1/record`.

## Blast radius

If an antipattern fires, call `scar_blast_radius` with the `error_id` (or `signature`) before touching importers.
